.TH "PERCH-MAIL-SEARCH" "1" "" "perch" "perch manual"
.SH NAME
perch\-mail\-search \- search message metadata
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B perch mail search [OPTIONS]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Search a mailbox with IMAP SEARCH and print metadata for matching messages. Results are newest first by default; \-\-reverse flips the order.
.PP
Bare query words search the message text. Supported keys: from, to, cc, bcc, subject, body, text, header:Name=Value, since, before, on, sent\-since, sent\-before, sent\-on, seen, unseen, answered, unanswered, flagged, unflagged, deleted, undeleted, draft, undraft, larger, smaller, uid, flag/keyword, and unflag/unkeyword.
.PP
Aliases: find.
.SH NOTES
.IP \(bu 2
The default limit is 50; \-\-limit 0 means unlimited.
.IP \(bu 2
The mailbox is examined read\-only, so search does not change flags.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-username, \-u <value>
account username (env PERCH_IMAP_USER)
.TP
.B \-\-password <value>
account password (prefer PERCH_IMAP_PASSWORD or \-\-password\-file)
.TP
.B \-\-password\-file <value>
read the account password from a file
.TP
.B \-\-password\-stdin
read the account password from stdin
.TP
.B \-\-timeout <value>
connection timeout (default: 30s)
.TP
.B \-\-config <value>
configuration file (default: ~/.config/perch/perch.yaml)
.TP
.B \-\-mailbox, \-m <value>
mailbox to search (default: "INBOX")
.TP
.B \-\-query, \-q <value>
search expression (see the examples in \-\-help)
.TP
.B \-\-uids <value>
explicit UID set, for example 1,3:5,10:*
.TP
.B \-\-limit, \-n <value>
maximum results (0 means unlimited) (default: 50)
.TP
.B \-\-reverse
oldest first instead of newest first
.TP
.B \-\-json
write one JSON object per message
.TP
.B \-\-server, \-s <value>
IMAP server (imaps://host, imap://host, or host[:port]); defaults from \-\-config
.TP
.B \-\-plaintext
connect to IMAP without TLS (use only on trusted networks)
.TP
.B \-\-starttls
require STARTTLS for IMAP
.TP
.B \-\-insecure
skip IMAP TLS certificate verification
.TP
.B \-\-ca\-file <value>
PEM CA bundle used to verify the IMAP server certificate
.TP
.B \-\-help, \-h
show help
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
perch mail search \-q 'from:alice since:2026\-01\-01'

perch mail search \-q 'unseen larger:1M' \-\-json

perch mail search \-\-uids 12,14 \-\-limit 0
.fi
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B PERCH_IMAP_USER
default account username
.TP
.B PERCH_IMAP_PASSWORD
account password
.SH SEE ALSO
.PP
\fBperch\fR(1), \fBperch\-mail\fR(1)
